{"_id":{"$oid":"5c46731208d98a02694c66c1"},"headword":"אט\"בח","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"A01069","refs":["Jastrow, א\"ט 1"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":" v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_א\"ט.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, א\"ט 1\">א\"ט</a>"}]},"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"אַטְבָּא","next_hw":"אַטְבְּעָא"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c46745008d98a02694c74dd"},"headword":"אַלֶּפְבֵּיתָא","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"A01940","refs":["Jastrow, אלפ\"א 1","Kohelet Rabbah 1:13"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":" m., pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">אַלֶּפְבֵּיתִין</span> same. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Kohelet_Rabbah.1.13\" data-ref=\"Kohelet Rabbah 1:13\">Koh. R. to I, 13</a>; v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_אלפ\"א.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, אלפ\"א 1\">אלפ\"א</a>"}]},"plural_form":[],"alt_headwords":[],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"אַלְפַבֵּטָרִין","next_hw":"אלפבתרין"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c4677dd08d98a02694c9e35"},"headword":"בִּית","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"B00752","refs":["Pesachim 107a:3","Sanhedrin 95a:5","Taanit 24b:6","Pesachim 42a","Berakhot 60b:13","Sanhedrin 63b:12","Sanhedrin 109a:2","Jastrow, בי\"ת 1","Eruvin 73a","Sanhedrin 47a:5"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":", inf. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_בּוּת.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, בּוּת 1\">בּוּת</a> (sec. r. of <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_בּוֹא.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, בּוֹא 1\">בוא</a>) <i>to go in, lodge, pass the night.</i> <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Daniel.6.19\" data-ref=\"Daniel 6:19\">Dan. VI, 19</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Onkelos_Genesis.32.22\" data-ref=\"Onkelos Genesis 32:22\">Targ. Gen. XXXII, 22</a>; a. fr.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Pesachim.107a.3\" data-ref=\"Pesachim 107a:3\">Pes. 107ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">בת טוות</span> (Dan. l. c.) he went to bed without tasting food. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sanhedrin.95a.5\" data-ref=\"Sanhedrin 95a:5\">Snh. 95ᵃ</a> (prov.) <span dir=\"rtl\">בת דינא וכ׳</span> if punishment is procrastinated, punishment is gone. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Taanit.24b.6\" data-ref=\"Taanit 24b:6\">Taan. 24ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ביתו כולי וכ׳</span> go ye all to bed fasting. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Pesachim.42a\" data-ref=\"Pesachim 42a\">Pes. 42ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מיא דביתו</span> (Chald. transl. of the ambiguous <span dir=\"rtl\">מים שֶׁלָּנוּ</span>) water kept in vessels over night. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Berakhot.60b.13\" data-ref=\"Berakhot 60b:13\">Ber. 60ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">בת בדברא</span> he slept in the open field. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sanhedrin.63b.12\" data-ref=\"Sanhedrin 63b:12\">Snh. 63ᵇ</a>.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sanhedrin.109a.2\" data-ref=\"Sanhedrin 109a:2\">Ib. 109ᵃ</a> top <span dir=\"rtl\">בעי למֵיבַת</span> he wanted to stay over night; a. e.—Part. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_בָּאִית.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, בָּאִית 1\">בָּאֵית</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Isaiah.58.5\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Isaiah 58:5\">Targ. Is. LVIII, 5</a>."},{"grammar":{"binyan_form":["בַּיֵּית"],"verbal_stem":"Pa."},"senses":[{"definition":" <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_בי\"ת.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, בי\"ת 1\">same</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Eruvin.73a\" data-ref=\"Eruvin 73a\">Erub. 73ᵃ</a> (opp. to taking meals)."}]},{"grammar":{"binyan_form":["אָבִית"],"verbal_stem":"Af."},"senses":[{"definition":"<i>to keep over night, postpone burial</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sanhedrin.47a.5\" data-ref=\"Sanhedrin 47a:5\">Snh. 47ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵבִית ליה למת</span> dare one postpone the burial of the dead?"}]}]},"plural_form":[],"alt_headwords":["בָּת"],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"בי\"ת","next_hw":"בַּיִת"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c4677de08d98a02694c9e8d"},"headword":"בי\"תא","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"B00757","refs":["Jastrow, בי\"ת 1"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":", v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_בי\"ת.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, בי\"ת 1\">בי\"ת</a>"}]},"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"בַּיְתָא","next_hw":"בַּיְתוֹס"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c467ccd08d98a02694cdbd9"},"headword":"דכ\"ץ","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"D00791","refs":["Jastrow, אח\"ס 1","Shabbat 104a:12"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":", v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_אח\"ס.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, אח\"ס 1\">אח\"ס</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Shabbat.104a.12\" data-ref=\"Shabbat 104a:12\">Sabb. 104ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ד̇כים הם כ̇נים הם צ̇דיקים הם</span> they are humble, sincere, righteous."}]},"plural_form":[],"alt_headwords":[],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"דִּכְסָס","next_hw":"דְּכַר I"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c4679eb08d98a02694cb769"},"headword":"גּוּר I","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"C00473","refs":["Jastrow, ג\"ר 1","Sotah 36b:17","Bereishit Rabbah 94","Yevamot 96b","Shabbat 104a:11","Sifrei Devarim 301:3-4","Bereishit Rabbah 39","Shabbat 31a:5","Berakhot 57b:20","Yevamot 47b:5","Avodah Zarah 3b:3"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":" (b. h.) [<i>to move around</i> (cmp. <span dir=\"rtl\">סחר</span>),] <i>to be a stranger, sojourn, dwell</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sotah.36b.17\" data-ref=\"Sotah 36b:17\">Sot. 36ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">גֹרֹא שגָֹּרֹ וכ׳</span> he is named Gera (<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Genesis.46.21\" data-ref=\"Genesis 46:21\">Gen. XLVI, 21</a>), because he (Joseph) dwells in exile; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bereishit_Rabbah.94\" data-ref=\"Bereishit Rabbah 94\">Gen. R. s. 94</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Yevamot.96b\" data-ref=\"Yevamot 96b\">Yeb. 96ᵇ</a> is it possible <span dir=\"rtl\">לָגּוּר וכ׳ בשני</span> to dwell (simultaneously) in two worlds? <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Shabbat.104a.11\" data-ref=\"Shabbat 104a:11\">Sabb. 104ᵃ</a>, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_ג\"ר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, ג\"ר 1\">ג\"ר</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sifrei_Devarim.301.3-4\" data-ref=\"Sifrei Devarim 301:3-4\">Sifré Deut. 301</a> (ref. to <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.26.5\" data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 26:5\">Deut. XXVI, 5</a>) <span dir=\"rtl\">מלמד … להשתקע אלא לָגוּר שם</span> it proves that he (Jacob) did not go down to be permanently settled, but only to sojourn there; a. fr.—Denom. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גֵּר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גֵּר 1\">גֵּר</a>."},{"grammar":{"binyan_form":["גִּיֵּיר"],"verbal_stem":"Pi."},"senses":[{"definition":" (denom. of <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גֵּר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גֵּר 1\">גֵּר</a>) <i>to make a proselyte, to initiate into the Jewish faith</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bereishit_Rabbah.39\" data-ref=\"Bereishit Rabbah 39\">Gen. R. s. 39</a> (ref. to <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Genesis.12.5\" data-ref=\"Genesis 12:5\">Gen. XII, 5</a> ‘the souls which they had made’) <span dir=\"rtl\">אלו הגרים שגִּיְּירוּ</span> that means the proselytes they had made. Ib. <span dir=\"rtl\">כל מי שמקרב … ומְגַיְּירוֹ וכ׳</span> whoever befriends a gentile and effects his conversion, is considered as though he had created him. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Shabbat.31a.5\" data-ref=\"Shabbat 31a:5\">Sabb. 31ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">גַּיְּירֵנִי וכ׳</span> make me a Jew with the condition &c.; a. fr. [For <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גִּיֵּיר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גִּיֵּיר 1\">גִּיֵּיר</a> <i>to dress with lime</i>, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גִּיר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גִּיר 1\">גִּיר</a>.]"}]},{"grammar":{"binyan_form":["הִתְגַּיֵּיר",""],"verbal_stem":"Hithpa."},"senses":[{"definition":", <i>Nithpa</i>. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גִּיֵּיד.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גִּיֵּיד 1\">נִתְגַּיֵּיר</a> <i>to become a proselyte</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Berakhot.57b.20\" data-ref=\"Berakhot 57b:20\">Ber. 57ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">עתידים להִתְגַּיֵּיר</span> they will adopt the Jewish faith. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Yevamot.47b.5\" data-ref=\"Yevamot 47b:5\">Yeb. 47ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">גר שבא להתג׳</span> if a stranger comes (appears before Jewish authorities) desirous to become a Jew. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Avodah_Zarah.3b.3\" data-ref=\"Avodah Zarah 3b:3\">Ab. Zar. 3ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מִתְגַּיְּירִין</span> shall ask to be admitted &c.; a. fr."}]}]},"plural_form":[],"alt_headwords":[],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"גּוּצִין","next_hw":"גּוּר"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c467b5008d98a02694cc79b"},"headword":"ג\"ר","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"C01224","refs":["Jastrow, א\"ת 1","Shabbat 104a:10","Shabbat 104a:11"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":", a transmutation of letters, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_א\"ת.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, א\"ת 1\">א\"ת</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Shabbat.104a.10\" data-ref=\"Shabbat 104a:10\">Sabb. 104ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">גוֹפו טימא אר̇חם עליו</span> though he defiled his body, I shall have mercy &c. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Shabbat.104a.11\" data-ref=\"Shabbat 104a:11\">Ib.</a> <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_ג\"ר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, ג\"ר 1\">ג\"ר ד\"ק</a>: <span dir=\"rtl\">אם … ג̇ור̇ בד̇וק̇</span> (Ar. <span dir=\"rtl\">גֵֹּר̇ בד̇וק̇ תהיה</span>) if thou doest so (be chaste), dwell thou in heaven (a dweller … shalt thou be)."}]},"plural_form":[],"alt_headwords":["ג\"ר ד\"ק"],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"גקרמונין","next_hw":"גֵּר"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c467b5008d98a02694cc79f"},"headword":"גֵּר","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"C01225","language_code":"(b. h.;","refs":["Jastrow, גּוּר 1","Jastrow, ג\"ר 1","Shabbat 104a:10","Shabbat 104a:11","Yevamot 46b:6","Yevamot 46b:9","Yevamot 46b:10","Yevamot 46b:14","Yevamot 46b:15","Yevamot 46b:16","Yevamot 46b:17","Berakhot 47b:12","Kiddushin 62b:1","Sanhedrin 96b:8","Gittin 57b:6","Avodah Zarah 3b:3","Avodah Zarah 3b:4","Avodah Zarah 24a:15","Avodah Zarah 24a:17","Chullin 3b:17","Kiddushin 75b","Sanhedrin 85b:24","Yevamot 24b:3","Yevamot 24b:4","Yevamot 24b:6","Yevamot 24b:8","Niddah 56b:30","Niddah 56b:35","Niddah 56b:37","Bava Metzia 58b:6","Bava Metzia 58b:8","Shabbat 33b:5","Yevamot 47a:5","Bamidbar Rabbah 8:1","Bamidbar Rabbah 8:2","Bamidbar Rabbah 8:3","Bamidbar Rabbah 8:4","Bamidbar Rabbah 8:9","Niddah 13b:22","Pesachim 87b:14","Bereishit Rabbah 88:1","Bereishit Rabbah 88:2","Bereishit Rabbah 88:3","Bereishit Rabbah 88:4","Bereishit Rabbah 88:5","Bereishit Rabbah 88:6","Bereishit Rabbah 88:7","Jerusalem Talmud Bava Metzia 5:5:4"],"language_reference":" <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גּוּר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גּוּר 1\"><a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גּוּר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גּוּר 1\">גּוּר</a>)</a>","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<i>a dweller</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Shabbat.104a.11\" data-ref=\"Shabbat 104a:11\">Sabb. 104ᵃ</a>, v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_ג\"ר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, ג\"ר 1\">preced.</a>","number":"1)"},{"definition":"<i>a stranger</i>. Tanḥ. Vayigg. 4 <span dir=\"rtl\">גרא שנעשה ג׳</span> he is named Gera, because he (Joseph) became a stranger, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גּוּר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גּוּר 1\">גּוּר</a>.—Esp. <i>a proselyte, convert to Judaism</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Yevamot.46b.17\" data-ref=\"Yevamot 46b:17\">Yeb. 46ᵇ</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Berakhot.47b.12\" data-ref=\"Berakhot 47b:12\">Ber. 47ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">לעולם אינו ג׳ וכ׳</span> one is not a proselyte until he has been &c. Yeb. l. c.; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Kiddushin.62b.1\" data-ref=\"Kiddushin 62b:1\">Kidd. 62ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳ צריך שלשה</span> a proselyte requires a court of three for making declaration and immersion. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Keritot.2.1\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Keritot 2:1\">Kerith. II, 1</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳ מחוסר כפרה</span> a proselyte who has not yet offered a sacrifice in the Temple; a. v. fr.—<span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳ צֶדֶק</span> a full, true proselyte, <span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳ תֹּושָׁב</span> one who, for the sake of acquiring limited citizenship in Palestine, renounces idolatry. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sanhedrin.96b.8\" data-ref=\"Sanhedrin 96b:8\">Snh. 96ᵇ</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Gittin.57b.6\" data-ref=\"Gittin 57b:6\">Gitt. 57ᵇ</a>; a. fr.—<span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳ שקר</span> an insincere proselyte (from impure motives). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Bava_Metzia.5.5.4\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Bava Metzia 5:5:4\">Y. B. Mets. V, 10ᶜ</a>.—Pl. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גְּרַם II.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גְּרַם II 1\">גֵּרִים</a>, constr. <span dir=\"rtl\">גֵּרֵי</span>, <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גֵּירִי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גֵּירִי 1\">גֵּירֵי</a>.—<span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳ גרורים</span> self-made converts, not formally admitted. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Avodah_Zarah.3b.4\" data-ref=\"Avodah Zarah 3b:4\">Ab. Zar. 3ᵇ</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Avodah_Zarah.24a.17\" data-ref=\"Avodah Zarah 24a:17\">24ᵃ</a>; a. e.—גרי אריות <i>lion-proselytes</i>, i.e. proselytes from mere fear (with ref. to <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/II_Kings.17.25\" data-ref=\"II Kings 17:25\">II Kings XVII, 25</a> sq.). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Chullin.3b.17\" data-ref=\"Chullin 3b:17\">Ḥull. 3ᵇ</a>, opp. <span dir=\"rtl\">גרי אמת</span>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Kiddushin.75b\" data-ref=\"Kiddushin 75b\">Kidd. 75ᵇ</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sanhedrin.85b.24\" data-ref=\"Sanhedrin 85b:24\">Snh. 85ᵇ</a>; a. fr.—<span dir=\"rtl\">גרי חלומות</span> proselytes converted by the advice of a dreamer or an interpreter of dreams; <span dir=\"rtl\">גרי מרדכי ואסתר</span> such as joined the Jewish ranks from motives like those prevalent in the days of Mordecai and Esther (<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Esther.8.17\" data-ref=\"Esther 8:17\">Esth. VIII, 17</a>). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Yevamot.24b.8\" data-ref=\"Yevamot 24b:8\">Yeb. 24ᵇ</a>.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Niddah.7.3\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Niddah 7:3\">Nidd. VII, 3</a> (<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Niddah.56b.37\" data-ref=\"Niddah 56b:37\">56ᵇ</a>) <span dir=\"rtl\">גרים טועין</span> Ar. (ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">וטועין</span>) proselytes not living in accordance with the Jewish usages.—<span dir=\"rtl\">בן גרים</span> a descendant of proselytes. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Bava_Metzia.4.10\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Bava Metzia 4:10\">B. Mets. IV, 10</a> (<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Metzia.58b.8\" data-ref=\"Bava Metzia 58b:8\">58ᵇ</a>).—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Shabbat.33b.5\" data-ref=\"Shabbat 33b:5\">Sabb. 33ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">יהודה בן ג׳</span>. [Mode of admission, v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Yevamot.47a.5\" data-ref=\"Yevamot 47a:5\">Yeb. 47ᵃ</a>.—Views about converts, v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bamidbar_Rabbah.8.9\" data-ref=\"Bamidbar Rabbah 8:9\">Num. R. s. 8</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Niddah.13b.22\" data-ref=\"Niddah 13b:22\">Nidd. 13ᵇ</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Pesachim.87b.14\" data-ref=\"Pesachim 87b:14\">Pes. 87ᵇ</a>; a. fr.]. Fem. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גרי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גרי 1\">גֵּרָה</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bereishit_Rabbah.88.7\" data-ref=\"Bereishit Rabbah 88:7\">Gen. R. s. 88</a>, end.—Usu. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גִּיּוֹרֶת.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גִּיּוֹרֶת 1\">גִּיֹּורֶת</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Ketubot.4.3\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Ketubot 4:3\">Keth. IV, 3</a>; a. fr.","number":"—2)"}],"morphology":"m."},"plural_form":["גֵּרִים",""],"alt_headwords":[],"quotes":[[null,"גרי אריות",null]],"prev_hw":"ג\"ר","next_hw":"גְּרָא"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c467c7c08d98a02694cd72b"},"headword":"דְּיוֹר","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"D00541","refs":["Yoma 2a","Jerusalem Talmud Eruvin 5:7:6"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":" (<a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_דּוּר I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, דּוּר I 1\">דור</a>) <i>dwelling</i>, esp. <i>temporary residence, lodging</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Eruvin.5.7.6\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Eruvin 5:7:6\">Y. Erub. V, 23ᵃ</a> top <span dir=\"rtl\">לשם דייר</span> as a lodging place; a. e.—Pl. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_דְּיוֹסוֹס.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, דְּיוֹסוֹס 1\">דְּיוֹרִים</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">דְּיוֹרִין</span>. Ib. <span dir=\"rtl\">ד׳ ממש</span> real lodging places, <span dir=\"rtl\">ראוי׳ לד׳</span> fit for shelter. Tosef. ib. X (VII), 12; a. fr. V. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_דִּיר.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, דִּיר 1\">דִּיר</a>."}],"morphology":"m."},"plural_form":["דְּיוֹרִים","דְּיוֹרִין"],"alt_headwords":["דְּיָיר"],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"*דְּיוּקְתָּא","next_hw":"דַּיּוֹר"}
