{"_id":{"$oid":"5c469fd308d98a02694e5387"},"headword":"פִּיתּוּחַ","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"Q00890","language_code":"(b. h.;","refs":["Yoma 2a:3","Jerusalem Talmud Niddah 3:3:5","Jerusalem Talmud Avodah Zarah 3:9:2"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":" פָּתַח <i>Pi.</i>) <i>incision, engraving, engraved design</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Niddah.3.3.5\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Niddah 3:3:5\">Y. Nidd. III, 50ᵈ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">פ׳ ידים ורגלים וכ׳</span> it (the embryo) has no incisions indicating the outlines of hands and of feet. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Avodah_Zarah.3.9.2\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Avodah Zarah 3:9:2\">Y. Ab. Zar. III, 43ᵇ</a> bot. <span dir=\"rtl\">הומר היא בפ׳</span> the law is stricter in the case of an engraving made on a tree (Asherah).—Pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">פִּיתּוּחִים</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">פִּיתּוּחִין</span>, <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_פִּיתּוּחַ.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, פִּיתּוּחַ 1\">פִּתּ׳</a>. Ib. <span dir=\"rtl\">העכיר את הפ׳</span> if he effaced the engraving. Ohol. XIV, 1 <span dir=\"rtl\">העטרות והפ׳</span> the wreaths and engravings (mouldings above the entrance); Tosef. ib. XIV, 10 <span dir=\"rtl\">הפִּתּוּיִין</span>."}],"morphology":"m."},"plural_form":["פִּיתּוּחִים","פִּיתּוּחִין","פִּתּ׳"],"alt_headwords":["פִּתּ׳"],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"פִּיתְגָּם","next_hw":"פִּיתּוּחָא"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c469d9608d98a02694e3e5c"},"headword":"עֶרֶס","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"P01404","language_code":" ch. ","refs":["Jastrow, עֶרֶס II 1","Targum Jerusalem, Exodus 21:18","Sanhedrin 20a:13","Sanhedrin 20a:14","Sanhedrin 20a:15","Sanhedrin 20a:16","Nedarim 56b:2","Nedarim 56b:2","Bava Batra 22a:12","Vayikra Rabbah 5:3","Gittin 6a:17","Eruvin 26a","Shabbat 60a","Jerusalem Talmud Kilayim 9:3:15","Jerusalem Talmud Ketubot 12:3:15","Jerusalem Talmud Berakhot 3:1:8","Jerusalem Talmud Beitzah 1:7:2"],"content":{"senses":[{},{"definition":" <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עֶרֶס II.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עֶרֶס II 1\">same</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Onkelos_Deuteronomy.3.11\" data-ref=\"Onkelos Deuteronomy 3:11\">Targ. O. Deut. III, 11</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Onkelos_Exodus.7.28\" data-ref=\"Onkelos Exodus 7:28\">Targ. O. Ex. VII, 28</a>. Targ. Y. II ib. XXI, 18; a. fr.—<a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_תַּשְׁמִישׁ.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, תַּשְׁמִישׁ 1\">תשמיש</a> (<a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_ד.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, ד 1\">ד</a>)ע׳ <i>sexual connection</i>. Targ. Y. II ib. XIX, 15 (Y. I <span dir=\"rtl\">דעָרִיס</span>). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Numbers.5.13\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Numbers 5:13\">Targ. Y. Num. V, 13</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">דעריס</span>; a. e.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_II_Samuel.3.31\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on II Samuel 3:31\">Targ. II Sam. III, 31</a> <i>bier</i>.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Sanhedrin.20a.16\" data-ref=\"Sanhedrin 20a:16\">Snh. 20ᵃ</a>; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Nedarim.56b.2\" data-ref=\"Nedarim 56b:2\">Ned. 56ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳ דגדא</span>, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_גָּד ³.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, גָּד ³ 1\">גַּדָּא</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Nedarim.56b.2\" data-ref=\"Nedarim 56b:2\">Ib.</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳ דצלא</span> a bed with a leather mattress. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Eichah_Rabbah.1.1\" data-ref=\"Eichah Rabbah 1:1\">Lam. R. to I, 1</a> <span dir=\"rtl\"><a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_ע׳.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, ע׳ 1\">ע׳</a> (<a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_רַבָּתִי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, רַבָּתִי 1\">רבתי</a>) <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_פְּחִית.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, פְּחִית 1\">פחיתא</a></span> a broken bedstead. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bava_Batra.22a.12\" data-ref=\"Bava Batra 22a:12\">B. Bath. 22ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">לעַרְסֵיה וכ׳</span> waiting for the bier of R. A. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Kilayim.9.3.15\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Kilayim 9:3:15\">Y. Kil. IX, 32ᶜ</a> bot.; <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Ketubot.12.3.15\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Ketubot 12:3:15\">Y. Keth. XII, 35ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">יהבון עַרְסִי וכ׳</span> place my bier (coffin) at the sea-shore; a. fr.—Pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַרְסָן</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">עַרְסָתָא</span>, <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עַרְסִי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עַרְסִי 1\">עַרְסִין</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Targum_Jonathan_on_Amos.6.4\" data-ref=\"Targum Jonathan on Amos 6:4\">Targ. Am. VI, 4</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">עַרְסַתְהוֹן</span> ed. Lag. (oth. ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַרְסֵיהוֹן</span>). Lam. R. l. c. <span dir=\"rtl\">אתקין … עַרְסָאתָא</span> he prepared for them four beds. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Vayikra_Rabbah.5.3\" data-ref=\"Vayikra Rabbah 5:3\">Lev. R. s. 5</a> (transl. <span dir=\"rtl\">מטות שן</span> Am. l. c.) <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳ דפיל</span> ivory bedsteads. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Berakhot.3.1.8\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Berakhot 3:1:8\">Y. Ber. III, 6ᵃ</a> top <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳ קיסרייתא וכ׳</span> Cæsarean bedsteads which have holes for the girths; a. e.","number":"1)"},{"definition":" (cmp. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עָרִיס I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עָרִיס I 1\"><span dir=\"rtl\">עָרִיס</span> I</a>) <i>arcade along a row of buildings, sidewalk</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Gittin.6a.17\" data-ref=\"Gittin 6a:17\">Gitt. 6ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מצריך מע׳ לע׳</span> required identification of signatures on documents brought from one side of the street to the other. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Beitzah.1.7.2\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Beitzah 1:7:2\">Y. Bets. I, 60ᶜ</a> bot. <span dir=\"rtl\">מע׳ לע׳</span> from one side of the street to the other (or from one couch to the other, v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_טָעַן II.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, טָעַן II 1\"><span dir=\"rtl\">טְעַן</span> II</a>).—Pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַרְסָתָא</span>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Eruvin.26a\" data-ref=\"Eruvin 26a\">Erub. 26ᵃ</a> מערב … ע׳ ע׳ Ar. (Ms. M. <span dir=\"rtl\">ערסא ערסא</span>; ed. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַרְסְיָיתָא</span>, fr. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עַרְסִיתָא.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עַרְסִיתָא 1\">עַרְסִיתָא</a>) provided the whole town of M. with ‘Erubs (v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עֵירוּב.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עֵירוּב 1\">עֵירוּב</a>), one for each row of connected houses.","number":"—2)"},{"definition":"<i>dish of the steel-yard, scales</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Shabbat.60a\" data-ref=\"Shabbat 60a\">Sabb. 60ᵃ</a>, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עֲדָשָׁה.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עֲדָשָׁה 1\">עֲדָשָׁה</a>.","number":"—3)"}]},"plural_form":["עַרְסָן","עַרְסָתָא","עַרְסִין","עַרְסָתָא"],"alt_headwords":["עַרְסָא"],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"עֶרֶס II","next_hw":"עֲרִסָה"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c469e0308d98a02694e4228"},"headword":"פ\"א","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"Q00002","refs":["Jastrow, פ\"ה 1"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":" the letter <i>Pe</i>, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_פ\"ה.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, פ\"ה 1\">פ\"ה</a>."}]},"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"פ׳","next_hw":"פָּאבִי"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c46a86408d98a02694ea110"},"headword":"קַל II","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"S01230","language_code":"(b. h.;","refs":["Jastrow, קַל I 1","Yoma 85b:14","Rosh Hashanah 25b:2","Rosh Hashanah 25b:2","Arakhin 24a:39","Arakhin 18a:39","Pirkei Avot 5:20","Shabbat 80b:6","Bereishit Rabbah 16:4","Ketubot 112a:13","Ketubot 112a:14","Shemot Rabbah 19:5","Jerusalem Talmud Kiddushin 1:7:14"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":" <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_קַל I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, קַל I 1\">preced.</a>) <i>light</i>; "},{"definition":"<i>unimportant, of minor value; easy to achieve</i>.—<span dir=\"rtl\">קל וחומר</span>, v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_חוֹמֶר I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, חוֹמֶר I 1\"><span dir=\"rtl\">חוֹמֶר</span> I</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Chullin.12.5\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Chullin 12:5\">Ḥull. XII, 5</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מצוה ק׳ שהיא כאיסר</span> a slight religious act which is performed at a sacrifice of one Isar. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"Jerusalem_Talmud_Kiddushin.1.7.14\" data-ref=\"Jerusalem Talmud Kiddushin 1:7:14\">Y. Kidd. I, 61ᵇ</a> bot. <span dir=\"rtl\">השוה הכתוב מצוה ק׳ שבקַלּוֹת וכ׳</span> the Bible put the lightest of the light acts (<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.22.7\" data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 22:7\">Deut. XXII, 7</a>) on the same level with the most serious (<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Exodus.20.12\" data-ref=\"Exodus 20:12\">Ex. XX, 12</a>). Tosef. Yoma V (IV), 4 <span dir=\"rtl\">מאכילין אותו הקל הקל</span> you must give him to eat (of forbidden things on hand) that which is of comparatively minor import; a. fr.—Pl. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_קַלִּי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, קַלִּי 1\">קַלִּים</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">קַלִּין</span>; <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_קַלּוּת.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, קַלּוּת 1\">קַלּוֹת</a>.—<span dir=\"rtl\">קלים וחמורים</span>, v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_חוֹמֶר I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, חוֹמֶר I 1\"><span dir=\"rtl\">חוֹמֶר</span> I</a>.—<a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Demai.1.1\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Demai 1:1\">Dem. I, 1</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">הק׳ שבדמאי</span> those fruits with which, in cases of doubt as to tithes (v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_דְּמַאי.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, דְּמַאי 1\">דְּמַאי</a>), the law deals most leniently. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Yoma.8.8\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Yoma 8:8\">Yoma VIII, 8</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">על עבירות ק׳</span> for minor transgressions (to which the lowest penalty is attached); ib. 85ᵇ <span dir=\"rtl\">אלו הן ק׳ וכ׳</span> these are the minor transgressions: omission of a positive command &c. (v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_עָשָׂה.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, עָשָׂה 1\">עָשָׂה</a>); Tosef. ib. V (IV), 5. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Rosh_Hashanah.25b.2\" data-ref=\"Rosh Hashanah 25b:2\">R. Hash. 25ᵇ</a>, a. e. <span dir=\"rtl\">שלשה קַלֵּי עולם</span> the three worthless (chiefs) in Israel’s history, opp. <span dir=\"rtl\">חמורי עולם</span>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Rosh_Hashanah.25b.2\" data-ref=\"Rosh Hashanah 25b:2\">Ib.</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אפי׳ קל שבק׳ וכ׳</span> (not <span dir=\"rtl\">קלין</span>) even the most worthless of worthless men, if once appointed a leader, should be respected like the strongest &c.; a. fr.","number":"1)"},{"definition":"<i>lowly, poor.</i>—<i>Pl.</i> as ab. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Arakhin.24a.39\" data-ref=\"Arakhin 24a:39\">Arakh. 24ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">שלא ישהא מרגלית לק׳</span> one must not delay the valuation of a jewel dedicated for its value by poor men (for the sake of taking it to a large town where a higher price can be obtained, but it must go by its local value); <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Arakhin.18a.39\" data-ref=\"Arakhin 18a:39\">ib. 18ᵃ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מרגלית לק׳</span> as to local valuation.","number":"—2)"},{"definition":"<i>quick</i>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Pirkei_Avot.3.12\" data-ref=\"Pirkei Avot 3:12\">Ab. III, 12</a>, v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_נוֹחַ II.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, נוֹחַ II 1\"><span dir=\"rtl\">נוֹחַ</span> II</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Pirkei_Avot.5.20\" data-ref=\"Pirkei Avot 5:20\">Ib. V, 20</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">הוי … קל כנשר וכ׳</span> be … swift as an eagle, and run like a deer to do the will of thy Father in heaven. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Mishnah_Shabbat.8.5\" data-ref=\"Mishnah Shabbat 8:5\">Sabb. VIII, 5</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ביצה ק׳ שבבצים</span> the lightest of eggs; expl. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Shabbat.80b.6\" data-ref=\"Shabbat 80b:6\">ib. 80ᵇ</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ק׳ לבשל</span> quick to boil; Y. ib. VIII, 11ᵇ top. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bereishit_Rabbah.16.4\" data-ref=\"Bereishit Rabbah 16:4\">Gen. R. s. 16</a>, v. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_חַד I.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, חַד I 1\"><span dir=\"rtl\">חַד</span> I</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Ketubot.112a.14\" data-ref=\"Ketubot 112a:14\">Keth. 112ᵃ</a> (ref. to <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jeremiah.3.19\" data-ref=\"Jeremiah 3:19\">Jer. III, 19</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">נחלת צבי</span>) <span dir=\"rtl\">מה צבי זה קל … ק׳ לבשל וכ׳</span> as the deer is the swiftest of beasts, so the land of Israel is the swiftest of all lands to ripen its fruits. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Shemot_Rabbah.19.5\" data-ref=\"Shemot Rabbah 19:5\">Ex. R. s. 19</a>, a. fr. <span dir=\"rtl\">לשעה קלה</span> after a short time; a. fr.—<i>Pl.</i> as ab. Gen. R. l. c.; a. e.","number":"—3)"}],"morphology":"f."},"plural_form":["קַלִּים","קַלִּין","קַלּוֹת"],"alt_headwords":["קַלָּה"],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"קַל I","next_hw":"קַל III"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c46b42308d98a02694f0d61"},"headword":"שֵׁשַׁךְ","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"U02063","refs":["Jastrow, א\"ת 1","Bamidbar Rabbah 18:21","Megillah 6a","Avodah Zarah 65a:3"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":" (b. h.) <i>Sheshach</i>, surname of Babylonia (supposed permutation of <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_בָּבֶל.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, בָּבֶל 1\">בבל</a> by Atbash, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_א\"ת.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, א\"ת 1\">א\"ת</a>). <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Bamidbar_Rabbah.18.21\" data-ref=\"Bamidbar Rabbah 18:21\">Num. R. s. 18</a><sup>21</sup>, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_א\"ת.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, א\"ת 1\">א\"ת</a>. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Megillah.6a\" data-ref=\"Megillah 6a\">Meg. 6ᵃ</a>, v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_רַקַּת.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, רַקַּת 1\">רַקַּת</a>.","number":"1)"},{"definition":" <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_שאן.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, שאן 1\">בר ש׳</a> pr. n. m. <i>Bar Sheshach</i>, a Persian officer. <a class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Avodah_Zarah.65a.3\" data-ref=\"Avodah Zarah 65a:3\">Ab. Zar. 65ᵃ</a> Ms. M. (ed. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_שֵׁישַׁךְ.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, שֵׁישַׁךְ 1\">שֵׁישַׁךְ</a>).","number":"—2)"}],"morphology":"pr. n."},"plural_form":[],"alt_headwords":[],"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"שָׁשִׁיתָא","next_hw":"*שִׁשְׁעָה"}
{"_id":{"$oid":"5c46b4e408d98a02694f102a"},"headword":"תבט\"ש","parent_lexicon":"Jastrow Dictionary","rid":"V00042","refs":["Jastrow, תבש\"ט 1"],"content":{"senses":[{"definition":", v. <a dir=\"rtl\" class=\"refLink\" href=\"/Jastrow,_תבש\"ט.1\" data-ref=\"Jastrow, תבש\"ט 1\">תבש\"ט</a>"}]},"quotes":[],"prev_hw":"תֵּבוּתָא","next_hw":"תַּבֵּיב"}
